                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>Zara or H&amp;M — which is more successful?</h3>
                                        <p>Zara larger in absolute revenue ($40B vs $25B) but H&M has higher digital-first revenue share historically. Different strategies producing different outcomes.</p>
                                        <h3>Can smaller brands replicate Zara's speed?</h3>
                                        <p>The philosophy yes (fast supply chain + design cycles). The infrastructure no. Copy the discipline; adapt the scale.</p>
                                        <h3>Is H&amp;M's sustainability positioning credible?</h3>
                                        <p>Contested. Substantial investment but fast-fashion overall throughput draws criticism. Long-term commitment with mixed reception.</p>
                                        <h3>What is the biggest fast-fashion lesson?</h3>
                                        <p>Choose your moat (operations or brand marketing) and invest deeply. Trying to do both moderately underperforms committing to one.</p>
